Verdict: PASS. It's written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

• Intent: The new src/temperature_support.rs reads the Claude version (major, minor) from the model id as numbers instead of using a hand-written list. For Bedrock it uses yoagent's existing ModelConfig::bedrock_anthropic_id mapper and doesn't add a second one. Providers other than anthropic and bedrock are left alone.
• Real binary: I ran it with a fake key and a dead base URL.
  • --temperature 0.5 --model claude-opus-5-5 printed the stderr note once, then the expected connection-refused error.
  • The same command with --model claude-haiku-4-5 printed no note.
• Wiring: effective_temperature replaces the old assignment in build_agent, build_side_agent and build_architect_agent. The architect is checked against its own model, not the main one. I didn't read build_editor_agent in full: it copies the config with the editor model, and the builder test showing it drops temperature for claude-haiku-5-5 passes. The flag and .yoyo.toml both set the same AgentConfig.temperature field, so both are covered.
• Unused code: none. Every new function is called within this diff, and the REPL startup banner now says "(not sent: Claude 4.7+)" for models that reject it.
• Docs: installation.md now has the example temperature commented out with a caveat, skills.md gained the sentence about Claude 4.7 and later, and CHANGELOG.md has a Fixed entry.
• Product safety: older models still get the temperature they're configured with, so no working setup loses anything.

